  "query_preview": "and is now in effect until 8 pm Sunday.\n\nDangerous heat will continue across the area heading into early next \nweek. Monday and Tuesday look to be the hottest days of the extended \nperiod with several locations reaching the 100 degree mark. There is \na possibility that a few locations may reach 103 degrees and we may \nsee some new record highs being set, especially if the warmer \nguidance overperforms. \n\nThere is a chance that portions of the \"Elevated\" risk could get \nupgraded to a \"Significant\" risk for dangerous heat where heat \nindices could exceed above 110 degrees as we get closer to Monday. \nAn extreme heat warning may eventually be needed for portions of the \narea for Monday and Tuesday. Additional heat headlines and \nadvisories/warnings may eventually be introduced as we get closer to \nthe mid-week.\n\nRegarding the rain chances, they are mostly non-existent until early \nnext week. At that time, global guidance continues to show a signal \nfor deeper moisture in the westerlies north of the high center to \ncirculate around the high and potentially increase convective \nrainfall chances over eastern portions of the forecast area. Rain \nchances could be further increased by an approaching frontal \nboundary, but any relief from the heat that could result remains \nuncertain at this time. /CR/",
